# secrets — never commit
.env*
*.key
*.pem
.secrets*
*_SECRET*
*_API_KEY*
# ...but not test MODULES about secrets. core.ignorecase=true (the macOS default)
# makes *_SECRET* match test_secrets_arms.py, which git then drops from `add -A`
# SILENTLY — the #248 secrets-arm suite was the first source file to ever collide
# with these patterns, and more are coming (the keychain arm, the container floor).
# Filename patterns cannot judge content anyway; gitleaks scans contents and is the
# real guard. Keep this negation narrow: test modules under safe_agents/ only.
!safe_agents/**/test_*.py
# python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
# Per-epic session plans are TRACKED (convention change 2026-07-20). They carry
# structural claims later sessions read cold and act on ("X is the only writer",
# "Y is already built"), so they need git blame like any other asserted fact —
# an unverified claim must not be indistinguishable from a checked one forever.
# Claims in these files are tagged [verified <date>: <cmd>] / [assumed] / [ruling: <src>].
# EPICS.md is tracked for the same reason (un-ignored 2026-07-21) — the 2026-07-20
# change removed the NEXT_SESSION-* entries but left this one, so the portfolio
# snapshot kept making structural claims with no history. Nothing to add here.
# build/artifacts
.aws-sam/
*.zip
logs/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# Binary doc exports (keep the .md source of truth)
*.docx

# Local-only planning scratch (deliberately untracked — e.g. the org-migration
# what-moves/what-stays plan lives in MIGRATION-PLAN.local.md, 2026-07-24)
*.local.md

# Downloaded reference PDFs — re-downloadable, no binary bloat in git. The analysis
# lives in docs/references/ and cites the URL (2026-07-25).
research/CISA/
research/LangChain/

# Local Tests
local-tests/
